course: dictionary
lesson: 4507
title: One word, three meanings: haze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A haze is a thin mist, smoke or dust in the air that makes it hard to see far. «When New Horizons flew past Pluto, the world had a thin blue haze.» The clues are thin, blue and the way it hangs in the air, so haze must be something in the air that blurs your view.
explain: Haze can also be a feeling. «She was in a haze all morning, not quite awake.» The clue is not quite awake, so haze means a dreamy, confused state of mind. Always check: swap in mist and see if the sentence still makes sense. Here it does not, so you know this is a different meaning.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another place. In the US, to haze someone means to make new members do silly, embarrassing or dangerous things as a test. That is bullying, and it is against the rules. The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Haze means a thin mist, smoke or dust in the air that makes it hard to see far.
fact: «Haze» can also mean a confused or dreamy state of mind, as in «in a haze».
fact: «Smog» is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.
fact: Heat haze is the blurry look of the air on a hot day.
fact: In the US, to haze someone means to make new members do silly, embarrassing or dangerous things, and this is a kind of bullying.
exercise: «Pluto turned out to be a lively world with a thin blue haze.» What is the haze? | A solid wall of rock | A large plain of ice | A sea of water | *A thin mist or dust in the air
exercise: «Smog is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.» What does smog mean? | A heavy frost on the ground | *A dirty haze of smoke and car fumes | A clean, fresh breeze from the sea | A cloud that brings rain
exercise: «She was in a haze all morning, not quite awake.» What does haze mean here? | *A dreamy, confused state of mind | A thin mist over the fields | A bright light in the sky | A test of new members
test: «The new students were hazed with silly tasks as a test.» In this sentence, what does hazed mean? | A thin mist over the lake | *Made to do silly, embarrassing or dangerous things as a test | Lost in a dreamy state | Cleaned until they shone
test: Dad says the summer heat haze made the far hills blurry. What does heat haze do to the view? | It makes the sky turn dark at night | It makes the grass grow faster | *It makes distant things look blurry | It makes the sea freeze
exam: «Smog is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.» Which meaning of haze fits here? | *A thin mist, smoke or dust in the air | A bright light in the sky | A dreamy, confused state of mind | Making new members do silly tasks as a test
